  "environmentmanagement/environment-groups/add-environment-to-group": {
   "summary": "Environment Add",
   "notes": [
    "Adds a single environment (the path environmentId) to the group; there is no whole-list replace. The environment must already be a Managed Environment. The REST endpoint does not auto-upgrade it (the admin center does), and an unmanaged environment returns 400 InputValidationError.",
    "The success response is 202 Accepted with an undocumented Location header (shown below) pointing at the group operation to poll; see [Read Operation](#/operations/environmentmanagement_getEnvironmentGroupOperation). No Operation-Location or azure-asyncoperation header is sent.",
    "Membership is recorded on the environment record (its environmentGroupId), not as a members collection on the group. The 400 body is {error:{code:InputValidationError}}, not the documented ProblemDetails. Both api-version 1 and 2024-10-01 are accepted."
   ],
   "responses": {
    "202": {
     "headers": {
      "Location": {
       "description": "URL of the environment-group lifecycle operation to poll, of the form /environmentmanagement/environmentGroupOperations/{operationId}?api-version=1. Undocumented; verified against the live API.",
       "schema": {
        "type": "string",
        "format": "uri"
       }
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
